{title: Your Name (FJ_148_en)}
{subtitle: Dein Name}
{song_number: 148}
{language: en}
{tempo: 80}
{key: A}

{start_of_verse: 1}
As [A]morning dawns and [D]evening [E]fades,
You in[A]spire [D]songs of [E]praise [A]
that [A]rise from earth [D]to touch [E]Your heart [F#m7]and
[D]glorify [E]Your [A]Name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[A]Jesus, in Your [D]Name we [E]pray,
[A]come and [D]fill our [E]hearts to[A]day.
Lord, [A]give us strength [D]to [E]live for [F#m7]You and
[D]glorify [E]Your [A]Name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C#m7]Your [F#m7]Name is a [A]strong and mighty [D]tower;
[E]Your [F#m7]Name is a [A]shelter like no [D]other;
[E]Your [F#m7]Name, let the [A]nations sing it [D]louder,
'cause [C#m7]nothing has the [D]power to save
[Esus4]but Your [E]Name. [A]
{end_of_chorus}
